# Git commits

- Write commit subjects in the imperative mood ("add" rather than "added"). Use the body to explain why the change was made.
- One logical change per commit.
- Keep machine-specific settings out of commits.
- Don't force-push shared branches.
- Never add AI attribution to commits or pull requests. Omit agent or model co-author trailers and generated-with footers.

Why: reviewers use commit history to understand decisions, and contributors rely on shared branch history. The author of record owns the change.

